From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 01:28:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: implement non-seamless cube maps

A VK_EXT_non_seamless_cube_map sampler is served by sampling the same
storage through a 2D array alias of the constituent cube faces, so the
lowering turns a cube coordinate into a face and, for a cube array, the
array layer itself.

The cube a cube array coordinate selects is rounded and clamped against
the layer count the alias reports, and only then scaled by the six faces.
Vulkan clamps the cube against the cube count before the faces are
indexed, and clamping afterwards is not the same thing: a coordinate one
cube past the end would become an index six faces past the end, which
lands on the last face of the last cube instead of on the selected face
of it, and a coordinate below zero would collapse onto the first face of
the first cube the same way.

dEQP-VK.texture.shadow.cube_array.* sweeps the coordinate from just below
the first cube to well past the last one. In a native side by side
comparison against the seamless path, which Metal resolves natively, the
only differing texels are mip level choices near a face boundary, where
the lowered path evaluates the projected derivative per fragment instead
of across the quad; both lie inside the level range the reference allows.
---
